.TH DRAW 1.SH NAMEdraw \- a character-graphics drawing editor.SH SYNOPSIS\fBdraw\fR[\-n] [\-l=n] [\-w=n] file.SH DESCRIPTION\fBdraw\fRrules a canvas across the terminal and lets you draw on it in characters,saving the picture to\fIfile\fR.\fRYou move a cursor over the canvas and it lays down the currentcharacter as it goes:\fBh\fR,\fR\fBj\fR,\fR\fBk\fRand\fBl\fRmove,\fBp\fRlifts and drops the pen, backslash chooses the character, and\fB?\fRshows all the keys..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-l=\fIn\fRa canvas of\fIn\fRlines; 132 unless told..TP 12\fB\-w=\fIn\fRlines up to\fIn\fRcharacters wide; 80 unless told..TP 12\fB\-n\fRmove with the numeric keypad instead.